var FOUR=[
{t:["1. Kamwe usiache kumwamini na kumtumaini Mungu","1. Never stop believing and trusting God"],
 b:["Kuna nyakati utakutana na mambo magumu, huenda yakazidi uwezo wako: ada, upweke, mitihani, magonjwa, au kukosa msaada. Hapo ndipo imani yako inapoonekana. Mwamini na kumtumaini Mungu, naye atafanya.\nKumtumaini Mungu si kukaa bila kuchukua hatua. Ni kufanya wajibu wako kwa bidii huku moyo wako ukimtegemea yeye, si akili zako, wala marafiki, wala akiba yako pekee.","There will be times you meet hard things, perhaps beyond your strength: fees, loneliness, exams, sickness, or lack of help. That is where your faith shows. Believe and trust God, and he will act.\nTrusting God is not sitting idle. It is doing your duty diligently while your heart leans on him, not on your own understanding, your friends, or your savings alone."],
 r:[["Zaburi 37:5 — mkabidhi Bwana njia yako, mtumaini, naye atafanya.","Mithali 3:5-6 — usitegemee akili zako mwenyewe; katika njia zako zote mkiri yeye.","2 Wakorintho 12:9 — neema yake inakutosha katika udhaifu wako."],["Psalm 37:5 — commit your way to the Lord, trust in him, and he will act.","Proverbs 3:5-6 — do not lean on your own understanding; acknowledge him in all your ways.","2 Corinthians 12:9 — his grace is sufficient in your weakness."]],
 a:["Kila asubuhi andika jambo moja ulilomwomba Mungu, na jioni andika alivyokujibu.","Each morning write one thing you asked God for, and each evening write how he answered."]},
{t:["2. Kamwe usiache Neno la Mungu na utakatifu","2. Never leave God’s Word and holiness"],
 b:["Neno la Mungu hukupa nuru katika safari yako. Huondoa confusion (mkanganyiko) na mawazo yasiyo ya kweli, hukupa direction, na litakupa ufunuo utakaokuvusha kutoka hatua moja kwenda nyingine.\nUtakatifu unakupa access ya kumkaribia Mungu. Unamfanya Mungu awe sensitive na kilio chako, na unakusaidia kupata msaada haraka kwa sababu unakuwa katika uwepo wake. Dhambi hutenga; utakatifu huleta ukaribu.","God’s Word gives you light on your journey. It removes confusion and false thoughts, gives you direction, and brings revelation that carries you from one level to the next.\nHoliness gives you access to draw near to God. It makes God attentive to your cry and helps you receive help quickly, because you live in his presence. Sin separates; holiness brings nearness."],
 r:[["Zaburi 119:105 — Neno lako ni taa ya miguu yangu na mwanga wa njia yangu.","Yoshua 1:8 — litafakari Neno mchana na usiku, ndipo njia yako itafanikiwa.","Waebrania 12:14 — fuateni utakatifu, ambao bila huo hakuna atakayemwona Bwana.","Isaya 59:1-2 — dhambi ndizo zinazotenga kati yenu na Mungu."],["Psalm 119:105 — your word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my path.","Joshua 1:8 — meditate on the Word day and night, and your way will prosper.","Hebrews 12:14 — pursue holiness, without which no one will see the Lord.","Isaiah 59:1-2 — sins are what separate you from God."]],
 a:["Soma sura moja kila siku kabla ya simu, na utii jambo moja ulilojifunza.","Read one chapter daily before your phone, and obey one thing you learned."]},
{t:["3. Kamwe usiache maombi na utumishi","3. Never leave prayer and service"],
 b:["Maombi huvuta neema ya Mungu juu ya maisha yako. Hukupa hekima, ufunuo na msaada, hurahisisha jambo unalolifanya, na hukufikisha umbali ambao usingefika kwa nguvu zako.\nUtumishi humfanya Mungu akuheshimu. Ushuhuda wa Mwalimu: nimemtumikia Mungu nikiwa chuoni, na nakuambia kitu nilichokipitia na kukihakikisha: hutafeli, hutapata disco wala sup, haijalishi unapitia nini. Utumishi na masomo havipingani; soma kwa bidii kama kwa Bwana, na umtumikie popote ulipo.","Prayer draws God’s grace upon your life. It gives you wisdom, revelation and help, makes your work easier, and carries you farther than your own strength could.\nService makes God honor you. The Teacher’s testimony: I served God while at university, and I tell you something I lived and proved: you will not fail, no discontinuation, no supplementary exams, whatever you are passing through. Service and study do not compete; study diligently as for the Lord, and serve him wherever you are."],
 r:[["Yakobo 1:5 — mtu akipungukiwa hekima, na aombe kwa Mungu, naye atapewa.","Yeremia 33:3 — niite, nami nitakujibu na kukuonyesha mambo makubwa usiyoyajua.","Yohana 12:26 — anayenitumikia, Baba atamheshimu.","1 Samweli 2:30 — wanaoniheshimu nitawaheshimu.","Wakolosai 3:23 — lolote mfanyalo, lifanyeni kwa moyo kama kumfanyia Bwana."],["James 1:5 — if anyone lacks wisdom, let him ask God, and it will be given.","Jeremiah 33:3 — call to me and I will answer you and show you great things you do not know.","John 12:26 — whoever serves me, the Father will honor.","1 Samuel 2:30 — those who honor me I will honor.","Colossians 3:23 — whatever you do, work at it with all your heart, as for the Lord."]],
 a:["Tenga dakika 20 za maombi kila siku na utumike mahali pamoja kila wiki.","Set aside 20 minutes of prayer daily and serve in one place each week."]},
{t:["4. Uaminifu na uwajibikaji","4. Faithfulness and responsibility"],
 b:["Kumbuka wazazi wako. Waliamini ndani yako wakawekeza ndani yako. Kuna wakati walitoa hadi senti ya mwisho, kuna wakati walikopa, walijinyima starehe walizostahili ili wewe usome. Usiwaangushe. Linda imani yao kwako.\nUwe na marafiki sahihi. Epuka makundi ya wahuni na tabia zinazokurudisha nyuma.\nKumbuka darasa la kwanza mlianza wengi. Wengine walifia njiani katika safari ya elimu, wengi walifeli, wachache walipata neema. Katika hao wachache, Bwana alikuona akakupa neema ukaenda sekondari, na leo uko chuoni. Kuwa mwaminifu, mwonyeshe Mungu hakukosea kukuamini na kukupa nafasi hiyo. Ukiwa mwaminifu kwa nafasi hii, Bwana atakuamini kwa nafasi kubwa zaidi: ukiwa mwaminifu kwa mambo madogo, utaaminiwa kwa makubwa pia.","Remember your parents. They believed in you and invested in you. There were times they gave their last coin, times they borrowed, times they denied themselves comforts they deserved so that you could study. Do not let them down. Guard their trust in you.\nKeep the right friends. Avoid gangs of troublemakers and habits that pull you backward.\nRemember that in first grade many of you began together. Some fell along the way, many failed, few received grace. Among those few, the Lord saw you and gave you grace to go to secondary school, and today you are at university. Be faithful, and show God he was not wrong to trust you with that opportunity. If you are faithful with this opportunity, the Lord will trust you with a greater one: faithful in little, trusted with much."],
 r:[["Luka 16:10 — aliye mwaminifu katika lililo dogo ni mwaminifu pia katika lililo kubwa.","Kutoka 20:12 — waheshimu baba yako na mama yako.","Mithali 13:20 — aendaye na wenye hekima atakuwa na hekima.","1 Wakorintho 15:33 — mashirika mabaya huharibu tabia njema.","Luka 12:48 — aliyepewa mengi, atatakiwa mengi."],["Luke 16:10 — whoever is faithful in little is faithful also in much.","Exodus 20:12 — honor your father and your mother.","Proverbs 13:20 — walk with the wise and become wise.","1 Corinthians 15:33 — bad company ruins good character.","Luke 12:48 — to whom much is given, much will be required."]],
 a:["Mwandikie mzazi au mlezi ujumbe wa shukrani wiki hii, na upime marafiki watatu wa karibu: wanakujenga?","Send a parent or guardian a message of thanks this week, and assess your three closest friends: do they build you?"]}];
